# WS-113 — Registration middleware: permissions + resource-predicate + If-Match + ETag + System-actor callbacks

**Target repo:** `magiq-media`
**Depends on:** MM-100, MM-148, MM-150, MM-152, MM-049

## Problem

Spec [`api-conventions.md § Refusal precedence`](../../../../docs/spec/shared/api-conventions.md#refusal-precedence--state-before-the-resource-predicate) + [`api-permissions.md`](../../../../docs/spec/shared/api-permissions.md): every write route checks `IPermissionService.IsGranted(Permission, claims)` at the edge (`403 PermissionDenied`), then the handler checks the resource predicate per each `registration.api.md § Authorization` row (`403 NotResourceOwner`); preconditioned routes refuse `If-Match`-absent as `428 PreconditionRequired` and emit `ETag: W/"<AggregateVersion>"` on 2xx. Adapter callback routes (`/dispatch`, `/receipt`) additionally require `actor.ActorType == "System"` (bound to `RegistrationAdapter` platform-integration role) and refuse `User` with `SystemActorRequired 403` (MM-148).

Registration endpoints:

- Declare no permission.
- Run no resource match (owner = `OfficerId`; `.All` widens).
- No `SystemActorRequired` check on dispatch / receipt callbacks.
- Read no `If-Match`.
- Emit no `ETag`.
- `erase-personal-data` named `If-Match` exception per `api-conventions.md`.

## Scope

| Concern | Spec | Code |
|---|---|---|
| Permission check at edge | `IPermissionService.IsGranted(Permission, claims)` → `403 PermissionDenied` | not called |
| Resource-predicate guard | caller == `OfficerId` or `.All` | handler returns `DomainError.InvalidOperation` |
| `SystemActorRequired` on `/dispatch` + `/receipt` | `actor.ActorType == "System"` else `403 SystemActorRequired` | not enforced |
| `If-Match` on preconditioned routes | submit, resubmit, cancel, confirm, reject, revoke, dispatch, receipt, correct-reference, request-amendment, approve/reject amendment, attach-documents | not read |
| `428 PreconditionRequired` when `If-Match` absent | — | — |
| `412 VersionMismatch` on mismatch (MM-049) | current code answers `409` | — |
| `ETag: W/"<AggregateVersion>"` on 2xx + conditional-safe `GET` | not emitted | — |
| `erase-personal-data` `If-Match` exempt | named exception per `api-conventions.md` | — |

## What the spec requires

- Every write endpoint declares `[Permission(RegistrationPermissions.<Verb>)]`.
- Handler orders refusal: permission → exists (`404`) → state (`409`/`422`) → resource predicate (`403 NotResourceOwner`).
- `/dispatch` + `/receipt` require System actor: inbound filter refuses `User` with `403 SystemActorRequired` before permission check (platform-integration auth boundary).
- Preconditioned routes read `If-Match` → compare to `AggregateVersion` → `428` absent, `412` mismatch, `400` malformed. 2xx responses carry `ETag: W/"<version>"`.
- `erase-personal-data` route is the named `If-Match` exception (irreversible but explicitly exempt).

## Wire-visibility

- Breaking — permission checks + `If-Match` enforcement + 412 flip; dispatch/receipt reject `User` actors; `ETag` added.

## Scope boundary

- Endpoint + handler surface only.
- `RegistrationPermissions` constants class = this plan's scope.
- Platform-level `IPermissionService` wiring = MM-100 scope.
- `VersionMismatch` 409 → 412 flip = MM-049.
- Idempotency / pagination / ProblemDetails = covered elsewhere.
- `SystemActorRequired` error code emission = MM-148.

